WEBVTT

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:08.230
Jinko didn't release the ball.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:13.920
All right!

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:15.320
Let's convert this one!

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:20.490
We're making a lot of mistakes 
in all areas of our play today.

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:27.610
Sorry.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:15.000
<b>Episode 23 
My Friend Taught Me</b>

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.820
<b>Ikuta Inn</b>

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:31.220
Which one is it?

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:33.340
Is it this one?

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:36.050
Or... is it this one?

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:39.660
Dammit. Which one?

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.550
Just hurry up and pick a card already.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:49.450
No one falls for tricks 
that obvious anymore.

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:50.380
All right!

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:52.770
It's this one!

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.470
Ack! I drew the Old Maid!

00:02:57.470 --> 00:02:59.080
He actually fell for it?!

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:02.490
How can he get so excited 
over a game of Old Maid?

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:11.030
Okay, I win.

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:13.400
I lost.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.610
I'm tired.

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:17.130
Senpai, one more game!

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.380
Let's play one more game.

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:23.810
Shut up. How do you have so much energy?

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:25.390
Go do some training or something.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:29.540
Oharano, about this play...

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:32.440
What? But I just got to the good bit.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:48.290
<b>Ikuta Inn</b>

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:48.580
<b>Atsushi</b>

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:48.580
<b>Where are you?</b>

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:48.580
<b>I just left the hotel
 and I'm on my way.</b>

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.450
<b>You said you were 
feeling down.</b>

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:55.580
<b>Are you really that nervous?</b>

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:58.590
<b>It may be their second 
string, but it's still Ryoin.</b>

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:00.300
<b>You'll be fine.</b>

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:04.090
<b>You'll be fine.</b>

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:06.350
<b>You think so...?</b>

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:08.180
<b>If you're so worried...</b>

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.890
...want me to train with you?!

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:17.150
H-How long have you been standing there?

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:20.180
Since you came outside.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:21.470
Why?

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:24.660
I thought I'd surprise you.

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:29.030
Jeez, I jumped out of my skin.

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:31.310
Don't be mad.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:33.380
I came to see you, after all.

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:37.170
<b>Calling</b>

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:37.170
<b>Taira-senpai</b>

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:41.870
Hello?

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:45.750
<i>Miyuki! What are you doing?</i>

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:49.030
Ah, sorry. I'm at Jinko's inn.

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:53.250
<i>What?! You're at Jinko's inn?</i>

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:55.210
<i>Is Sekizan there?</i>

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:56.710
No, he's not here—

00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:58.280
<i>Where's Sekizan?</i>

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:02.720
<i>I've been calling him, but he won't answer!</i>

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.960
<i>Sekizan!</i>

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:07.200
<i>Sekizan, where—</i>

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:18.670
<b>Calling</b>

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:18.670
<b>Taira</b>

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:42.960
Matsuo.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:46.160
Come with me.

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:59.710
Just how much does 
Taira-senpai like Sekizan-san?

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:04.930
Our third-years are close, aren't they?

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:08.430
But if he's not answering his phone, 
does that mean it's unrequited?

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:18.730
Come to think of it, I think most of 
the third-years were out of the room.

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:21.360
Maybe they're having a meeting.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:25.990
This is their last year at Sugadaira. 
Maybe they're reminiscing.

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:27.240
Maybe.

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.120
You're okay with barley tea, right?

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:37.560
Thanks.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:49.630
There's someone inside!

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:53.700
It's too dangerous to go inside.

00:06:54.770 --> 00:07:00.400
Should I train by washing the laundry by 
hand instead of using a washing machine?

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:04.810
No, that'd just be doing 
the laundry, not training.

00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:06.220
Gion-kun?

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:09.770
What? Tree Trunk?

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:14.440
What are you guys... doing?

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:17.660
Kenji, what are you doing?

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:23.390
I was wondering if I could use this washing 
machine for some kind of training.

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:30.170
<b>Training</b>

00:07:23.390 --> 00:07:25.420
Using a washing machine to train?

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:28.510
I'm impressed, Kenji. That's a novel idea.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:30.170
<b>Novel</b>

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:30.170
Novel?

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:33.640
So what kind of training are you doing?

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:35.140
Yeah, something.

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:36.560
Yeah, but what kind of "something"?

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:39.470
Just "something," okay?

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:43.560
But no ideas are coming to me.

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:48.440
Perfect. You guys can think with me.

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:53.040
I know. How about scrum training?

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:54.020
Okay.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:55.950
Give it a try.

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:58.700
Like this?

00:08:01.070 --> 00:08:04.290
What if we turn on the washing machine?

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:06.640
Don't!

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:09.540
You think we should put 
detergent in it first?

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:12.050
That's not the problem.

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:14.840
Then let's think of something that 
doesn't use the washing machine.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:17.600
We're not going to use it?

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:19.960
How about my new idea?

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:28.940
<b>Training</b>

00:08:20.690 --> 00:08:22.310
I'm all ears.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:25.520
First, extends your arms out and up.

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:25.990
Okay.

00:08:25.990 --> 00:08:28.820
And we'll begin by stretching our backs.

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:30.480
Wait, no!

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:32.490
These are just radio exercises!

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:37.120
Wanna play, then?

00:08:46.030 --> 00:08:48.980
I want to do something more intense.

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:51.670
This isn't so bad once in a while.

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:55.220
I hope we can play against Keijo again.

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:58.390
If we're lucky, we might 
meet in the preliminaries.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:01.600
Preliminaries for what?

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:04.660
The national tournament.

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:06.350
The prefectural preliminaries
 for Hanazono.

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:09.270
Hanazono, huh? I wanna go!

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:13.030
I want to go, too, but it's not easy.

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:17.410
And you won't get to go 
unless you beat us.

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:21.790
Yeah. We'll <i>definitely</i> beat you.

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:27.770
Wanna play a game, then?

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:31.170
Kenji, try taking the ball from me!

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:35.180
Bring it on! Let's go, Tree Trunk!

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:36.400
Huh? What?

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:37.680
Wait!

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:40.160
Wait up!

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:42.180
Can't catch me, Kenji?

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:44.470
Give me the ball!

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:48.020
Too weak!

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:52.820
Yeah, that's more like it.

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:55.280
Sumiaki, run!

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:56.850
Wh-What?

00:09:56.850 --> 00:09:59.440
You're next up to run with the ball!

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:01.010
G-Got it.

00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:02.500
Oh no, you don't!

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:04.950
Sumiaki, over here!

00:10:06.670 --> 00:10:07.870
Dammit!

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:09.370
Over here, Kenji!

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:11.870
Sumiaki!

00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:13.010
Y-Yeah!

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:28.400
You won't beat me!

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:30.040
Sumiaki, pass!

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:30.910
Okay!

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:34.880
Over here, Kenji!

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:36.150
Dammit!

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:38.990
Get fired up! Hotter! Hotter!

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:42.620
What are they doing?

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:52.450
That wasn't training at all, but I feel great.

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:57.130
What's so funny?

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:05.780
I was just remembering
the first time you talked to me.

00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:11.140
Wow, you're huge!

00:11:11.140 --> 00:11:15.980
Why don't you join the rugby team?
After all, rugby's...

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:20.860
...a real blast!

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:34.750
What training were you guys doing?

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:37.620
Secret training. Right, Tree Trunk?

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:38.760
Yeah.

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:43.260
Anyway, Senpai, let's have 
another game of Old Maid!

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:45.510
Stop! Let me sleep!

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:50.930
Matsu-san, were you doing something?

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:55.490
We're playing Ryoin tomorrow. 
We had a meeting.

00:11:55.490 --> 00:11:57.260
Oh, right.

00:11:57.260 --> 00:12:00.940
Since all the third-years were missing,
I figured something was up.

00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:05.520
This is crazy. What if I'm a starter tomorrow?

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:06.880
You won't be.

00:12:06.880 --> 00:12:07.990
What was that?

00:12:09.460 --> 00:12:10.650
Ebumi.

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:12.620
Huh? What is it?

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:14.780
Did you go running again?

00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:16.110
Yeah.

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:17.750
Good for you.

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:19.870
What's wrong with you? Gross!

00:12:19.870 --> 00:12:22.370
Guys, get some rest tonight.

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:24.920
We've got an important game tomorrow.

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:26.510
Yes, sir.

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:29.370
I'm so nervous.

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:32.520
Let's go to bed.

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:33.580
Okay, let's hit the hay.

00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:34.810
Good night.

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:36.400
You're going to sleep?

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:54.040
<b>So happy to be
 receiving attention 
for once that 
he can't move</b>

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:54.040
<b>This looks like something
you'd see in a home
with a cat...</b>

00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:05.220
Gion!

00:13:06.570 --> 00:13:09.100
It's Kanagawa's number one flanker!

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:11.200
Long time, no see.

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:14.570
And why are you calling me that?
It's embarrassing.

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:17.490
Just call me Sekito-senpai.

00:13:17.490 --> 00:13:20.860
I'm working real hard on 
being a flanker right now.

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:23.690
Hey, Raita. Good to see you.

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:27.880
Hey, bro. You're as big as ever.

00:13:27.880 --> 00:13:30.110
Huh? What's going on?

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:34.490
You're here early, Jinko.

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:40.140
I'm Ryoin Academy's coach, Minamoto Kosei.

00:13:40.140 --> 00:13:41.380
Nice to meet you.

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:46.340
I'm Jinko's coach, Komori.

00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:50.890
I've heard about you. 
Mostly from Sagami's Kita-kun.

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:53.640
That guy...

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:57.520
Thank you so much for playing us today.

00:13:57.520 --> 00:14:01.420
It's fine. It's good timing.

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:04.790
And they may be our second string,
but they're still strong.

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:08.410
Of course. We look forward to playing you.

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:11.530
What? You're not playing?

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:14.210
I'm on the first team.

00:14:14.210 --> 00:14:16.080
But the second string's flanker is—

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:17.290
Sekito-san!

00:14:19.610 --> 00:14:20.680
Mikado.

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:26.070
This is Mikado Sho. A first-year flanker
who's going to be playing today.

00:14:26.070 --> 00:14:27.420
Seriously?

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:35.160
Sekito-san, who is this midget?

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:38.340
What? Who are you calling 
a "midget," you midget?

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:42.600
There are only short asses here right now.

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:47.190
Apparently, Mikado came to Ryoin 
because he looked up to me.

00:14:47.510 --> 00:14:51.830
Sekito-san, you're a hero 
for small guys like us.

00:14:51.830 --> 00:14:53.580
I admire everything about you.

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:56.480
Everything about you is cool. I love you!

00:14:56.480 --> 00:14:59.740
I call him BL-kun.

00:14:59.740 --> 00:15:03.190
I don't know what that means,
but I'll take it!

00:15:06.660 --> 00:15:11.130
Have a good game, 
you short ass first-year flankers.

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:36.280
All right! I'm starting!

00:15:36.590 --> 00:15:38.720
We're counting on you, Gion.

00:15:38.720 --> 00:15:41.290
Yes, sir. We'll definitely win!

00:15:47.700 --> 00:15:48.860
Don't worry about it.

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:50.690
Sekizan.

00:15:50.690 --> 00:15:53.360
You shouldn't be worrying 
about him right now.

00:15:56.030 --> 00:15:58.060
Let's make them remember...

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:01.140
...our name!

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:04.810
Hey, Ryujin. It's starting.

00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:08.520
Ryoin's ball. Kickoff!

00:16:15.580 --> 00:16:19.870
It's starting! Uncle, hurry up!

00:16:20.640 --> 00:16:23.850
I don't want to watch Jinko play.

00:16:23.850 --> 00:16:25.200
Hurry!

00:16:27.100 --> 00:16:28.430
Captain!

00:16:28.430 --> 00:16:30.460
Kick some ass!

00:16:33.110 --> 00:16:36.590
<i>He's small. I could knock him off his—</i>

00:16:42.630 --> 00:16:43.980
That's low.

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:49.980
Killer Sekito-san Tackle.

00:16:50.340 --> 00:16:52.280
What was that? So lame.

00:16:54.250 --> 00:16:57.070
Knock-on by Jinko! Advantage!

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:01.680
Advantage?

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:03.990
What <i>was</i> that tackle?

00:17:03.990 --> 00:17:06.080
Stop them, Jinko!

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:08.350
Jinko, stop them!

00:17:08.350 --> 00:17:10.230
Jinko, fight!

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:14.260
I didn't want to watch this.

00:17:17.660 --> 00:17:20.390
Stay down, nobodies.

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:29.810
Knock-on. Advantage!

00:17:30.220 --> 00:17:32.840
Form a scrum where Jinko knocked-on
the ball before the advantage.

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:36.470
You bastard!

00:17:36.470 --> 00:17:40.710
Don't come out of nowhere and
start copying Sekito-san, you punk!

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:48.700
I'm not copying him.

00:17:49.270 --> 00:17:50.900
My friend taught me that move.

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:57.110
Gion-kun, over here.

00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:00.960
Grab onto my back.

00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:03.850
I-It might be a little difficult...

00:18:04.380 --> 00:18:05.890
It'll be fine.

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:11.040
This feels weird.

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:13.230
Crouch.

00:18:13.610 --> 00:18:15.990
Bind. Set!

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:25.660
The ball's out!

00:18:30.560 --> 00:18:33.420
<i>Since #10 and #12 have darted to the left,</i>

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:35.980
<i>they'll either pass the ball
to the outside or kick.</i>

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:46.470
Their #13 came around from the back!

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:48.560
Well, this sucks.

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:50.810
He got through on the inside!

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:59.820
This is what it means to defend your turf!

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:02.570
Awesome!

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:07.970
They're so quick!

00:19:07.970 --> 00:19:10.000
Stop them, Jinko!

00:19:19.620 --> 00:19:20.910
I'll stop him.

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:45.530
You can't touch me!

00:19:46.170 --> 00:19:47.890
He jumped!

00:19:47.890 --> 00:19:49.540
What just happened?

00:19:49.980 --> 00:19:51.590
Not bad.

00:19:51.590 --> 00:19:53.290
You think so?

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:56.420
Crap! He's going to reach the 22-meter line!

00:20:06.820 --> 00:20:08.230
Kibi!

00:20:08.230 --> 00:20:10.000
Nice tackle!

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:12.210
See? He's nothing special.

00:20:12.780 --> 00:20:14.860
Which side are you cheering for?

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:17.440
Get the ball back!

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:18.940
Hey, ball!

00:20:21.380 --> 00:20:24.200
I can't see the ball. Get it—

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:25.730
Pile-up!

00:20:27.060 --> 00:20:30.000
Because Jinko was on top in that scrum, 
form another scrum, Jinko's ball.

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:35.210
All right. Kibi, nice job.

00:20:35.640 --> 00:20:38.280
What are you doing, Mikado?

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:39.210
Ow, ow, ow!

00:20:39.690 --> 00:20:41.640
Jeez, sorry.

00:20:41.640 --> 00:20:44.250
I was supposed to score.

00:20:45.620 --> 00:20:48.090
Gion-kun, it's another scrum.

00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:58.230
Their flanker is pretty good, huh?

00:21:02.360 --> 00:21:04.290
Don't worry about it and 
focus on the next play.

00:21:08.250 --> 00:21:11.740
Damn. Damn.

00:21:15.340 --> 00:21:16.790
Gion-kun...

00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:24.010
I hate that I don't stand a chance 
against big guys like you.

00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:30.890
